  "notes": "Measured from XA-VDH (A320, 2026-03-22, left side); XA-VMB (2026-03-08, right side from below) and XA-VBR (A321neo, 2025-10-18) agree. The circles are drawn as polygons in each part's space; the lime one straddles the fin root. Belly: white (XA-VMB). Many aircraft still wear the previous 'viva aerobus' scheme (standard-2018), repainted gradually; some show the new titles with older engines. The A321neo winglets carry white lettering ('VIVO' seen on XA-VBR's), not drawn. The small red mark on the engine cowling isn't identified. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on XA-VDH, placed by its doors and overwing exits: the title runs 0.162 to 0.313; it has no capitals, so type.xHeight 0.77 just states the measured lowercase (0.77 R) against the nominal cap height. The circles are now drawn smooth through their points.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation. The October 2024 rebrand (Viva Aerobus becomes Viva) replaced the 2018-era 'viva aerobus' scheme (standard-2018), still on part of the fleet."
